      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays are limping into the All-Star break, their first-half hopes derailed by a sloppy exit in San Diego. <strong>Hoffman blew a late lead as the Jays fell to the Padres 5-4 on Sunday</strong>, capping a three-game split that ended with two straight losses and a 45-51 record. Sitting fifth in the AL East, 12 games behind the division leader, the team has now lost two straight and is trending downward after winning just one of their last five. Dylan Cease, who nearly threw a no-hitter against the Giants with eight no-hit innings and 11 strikeouts, will start for the American League in the All-Star Game, but his regular-season relief can't mask the bullpen's recent implosion. The lineup showed flashes - Clement batting.296 with a.751 OPS - but inconsistency reigns. <strong>They face the White Sox at 7:15 PM ET on Friday, July 17, as the second half begins with a chance to reset</strong>.",
