        "body": "The hunt for diamonds begins in the summer heat, where the Toronto Raptors are no longer chasing wins but searching for the next cornerstone. <strong>Allen Graves is validating the Raptors' first-round gamble</strong> with a Summer League explosion: 22 points, 13 rebounds, three steals, and two blocks in Game 2, shooting 3-for-8 from deep. That's the kind of raw output a 46-36 team, which finished third in the Atlantic Division, needs to justify its draft investment [verified facts]. Graves isn't the only name on the radar - Summer League is where unproven picks either ignite or vanish, and Graves is already flashing the versatility this roster lacks. The front office isn't just watching; it's building, weighing free agent targets against cap flexibility to reshape a squad that's been in the same spot for too long. <strong>What to watch: Graves' next two games and whether the Raptors add a veteran wing before camp opens</strong>.",
